    "title": "SJ: 3-Alarm House Fire Displaces 4 Wednesday Afternoon - NewsBreak",
    "text": "Four people were displaced Wednesday following a house fire in San Jose, according to the Fire Department. The three-alarm fire was first reported at 2:37 p.m. at a single-story home in the 3300 block of Gavota Avenue. The fire also extended to a house next door, the Fire Department said. In addition to four people being displaced, four dogs and one cat were also displaced. One cat is also unaccounted for, according to the Fire Department. The cause of the fire is under investigation but doesn't appear suspicious, Battalion Chief Shawn Tacklind said. Copyright © 2025 Bay City News, Inc. All rights reserved. Republication, rebroadcast or redistribution without the express written consent of Bay City News, Inc. is prohibited. Bay City News is a 24/7 news service covering the greater Bay Area.",
